Each entry's type, enumerated values and grouped members are the
document's, from its clauses and AVP tables, and so are its M and V bits
where the document states them.

Not added here: Filter-Id, code 3805, named like the dictionary's code
11 of vendor 0; MAC-Address, code 3806, named like the dictionary's code
524 of vendor 0; Time-Window, code 3818, named like TS29.154's code
4204. Wireshark names each display filter field after its AVP, so two
entries named alike need one renamed, as Cx-User-Data and Sh-User-Data
are.

